soflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 03-07-2018, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T12:36:57-08:00","id":1192713,"title":"","content":"So how much new crunch is there, and in particular, does it do anything to clarify what you can get with a cult?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T13:13:11-08:00","id":1192732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1069057-night-horrors-enemy-action?p=1192712#post1192712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That moment in life that you need to choose between Demon's Night Horrors and Beast's Player Guide... allow me to quote Pandora Hearts and ask- what should I do? What should I do?.. Oh do you cook a wolf?<br /> <br /> But seriously, I have no idea which book to choose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm biased toward both, but I think it depends: BPG has lots and <i>lots </i>of new crunch and character ideas for Beast. It's very much a player's book. Enemy Action is all about antagonists and storyhooks -- very much an ST book. So it really depends on which role you're more interested in. And, naturally, which game you like better!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T13:59:10-08:00","id":1192753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1069057-night-horrors-enemy-action?p=1192396#post1192396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most Night Horrors books do that, just of different tiers.<br /> <br /> Beast was likely only different because it aside from Heroes and other Beasts there was nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wicked Dead was all about weird stuff, Wolfbane (is that what it was called?) introduced idigam, and Unbidden has lots of weird stuff, too. I'm surprised if Enemy Action is just stuff we've seen before, but if you're looking for weird God-machine stuff there's like two chapters worth in Demon STG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T14:28:38-08:00","id":1192774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1069057-night-horrors-enemy-action?p=1192732#post1192732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm biased toward both, but I think it depends: BPG has lots and <i>lots </i>of new crunch and character ideas for Beast. It's very much a player's book. Enemy Action is all about antagonists and storyhooks -- very much an ST book. So it really depends on which role you're more interested in. And, naturally, which game you like better!</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be the problem- I like both games more or less the same, and it has been awhile since I took part in a game as either of those options. Enemy Actions looks really interesting, at least from the preview. Brass and the Angel Maker sounds really great, as well as Lavadiel, Lutzow and Carta, or the False Demon, the Would be Colony, and, and...<br /> <br /> Well, everything just looks awesome. While I'm yet to buy this book, just from a brief look everything looks great and interesting. Kudos to all the writers :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T15:05:43-08:00","id":1192793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1069057-night-horrors-enemy-action?p=1192753#post1192753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wicked Dead was all about weird stuff,</div> </div> </div> </div>Wicked Dead was also one of <i>two</i> Night Horrors books for Vampire, and the other one was all about unusual &quot;normal&quot; Kindred \u2014 Immortal Sinners gave us the Butcher Worm, the mindlinked Greengrass couple, and the only published writeup of a Methuselah, along with the likes of Solomon Birch and the Unholy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wolfbane (is that what it was called?) introduced idigam, </div> </div> </div>Wolfsbane introduced full mechanics for the idigam, which had been present in the setting since the corebook right down to the packs of the Rockies still cleaning up the aftermath of the most powerful specimen yet encountered; this was also after two full chapters of characters and phenomena that fit into existing categories.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and Unbidden has lots of weird stuff, too. </div> </div> </div>Which is unsurprising, because a large part of Unbidden's shtick was showing that Awakened magic was not wholly in control of mages and Mage is the gameline with the widest spread of core phenomena to draw upon; by the same token, though, there's precious little in that book that can't be fit into an existing box with minimal massaging, which can be said for pretty much every Night Horrors book apart from Wicked Dead's specific placement as part of a two-book spread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm surprised if Enemy Action is just stuff we've seen before, but if you're looking for weird God-machine stuff there's like two chapters worth in Demon STG. </div> </div> </div>I'm still delving through the Beast PG at the moment, but I'm not just surprised by but immediately doubtful of the notion that Enemy Action lacks new content in any more meaningful sense than, say, the first two chapters of Wolfsbane did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T15:34:21-08:00","id":1192808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1069057-night-horrors-enemy-action?p=1192793#post1192793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wicked Dead was also one of <i>two</i> Night Horrors books for Vampire, and the other one was all about unusual &quot;normal&quot; Kindred \u2014 Immortal Sinners gave us the Butcher Worm, the mindlinked Greengrass couple, and the only published writeup of a Methuselah, along with the likes of Solomon Birch and the Unholy.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one was actually really good, and so I'm hoping Enemy Action will be like that. The Butcher Worm's devotion in particular, letting a vampire become something profoundly vast and freakish, works great with that one that lets you be full of ghoul animals and bugs proportionate to your size, and a lot of devotions in that one are great in general, whereas while Conquering Heroes has interesting new takes on heroes and concepts that push the envelope (hero dream labs and hero reality TV for starters) but very little in the way of crunchy bits that can be used to present special threat. The Insatiables, of course, steal the show by giving Beasts their own Strix-analogs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T15:46:40-08:00","id":1192824,"title":"","content":"Can someone give a brief description of &quot;Wednesday&quot;? I assume it doesn't just reference today but also something in Enemy Action?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited"